# Runtime database role for RLS enforcement
# ------------------------------------------
# The app can connect with a restricted role (NOSUPERUSER, NOBYPASSRLS) so that
# per-table Row-Level Security policies are enforced at the database level.
#
# - DATABASE_URL: Superuser connection used for migrations (the startup script
#   temporarily unsets RUNTIME_DATABASE_URL during migrate so schema changes use
#   the superuser role).
# - RUNTIME_DATABASE_URL: Restricted role URL for normal app queries.
#
# When RUNTIME_DATABASE_URL is set (runtime role), the app uses it for the
# default database connection. When unset during runtime serving, production.py
# raises a clear error instead of silently falling back to the superuser
# DATABASE_URL (fail-closed). During migrations, the deployment script unsets
# RUNTIME_DATABASE_URL so the superuser DATABASE_URL is used instead.
# See local.py and production.py for the implementation.
#
# The init SQL template (db/init.sql) creates the runtime role automatically
# in Docker Compose environments. For production deployments, the operator
# creates the role manually and sets RUNTIME_DATABASE_URL in the environment.
# See OPERATIONS.md for the operator setup guide.
RUNTIME_DB_ROLE = config("RUNTIME_DB_ROLE", default="{{ runtime_db_role }}")
# RUNTIME_DATABASE_URL is consumed directly in local.py and production.py
